<Base title="Privacy" description="What Rulebook collects, what stays in your browser, who else touches your data, and how to have it removed.">
<div class="wrap prose reader-intro"><PageIntro title="Privacy" summary="See what is stored in your browser, what signup sends and how to request deletion.">Privacy · {LEGAL_DATE}</PageIntro></div>
<div class="wrap prose"><h2>Collected and stored on our side</h2><p>Akshay Kothari operates Rulebook. For the email list, if you join the email list, we store your email address, the date and time you joined, and the version of the consent text you agreed to (<code>weekly-note-v1</code>). It lives in a database on Cloudflare, our host. The signup endpoint stores the subscription; it does not itself send email, and this application has no external mailing-service integration. Registration records interest in the weekly note. Delivery has no published schedule. We do not sell or share it.</p>
<h2 data-u="mt6">Stays in your browser</h2><p>Your Gate trades and rules, your plan, your watchlist, your widget choices and a short cache of delayed quotes are saved in your browser's own storage on your device. They are not sent to us and we cannot see or recover them. Clearing site data removes them, so download the Gate book and Plan with its deployment history separately. Those downloads do not include watchlists, widget choices or cached quotes.</p>
<h2 data-u="mt6">Not collected</h2><p>No accounts, no passwords, no payments, no cookies, no advertising or analytics trackers, no fingerprinting. Fonts, scripts and both charting libraries (Lightweight Charts and uPlot) are served from this site; the page makes no requests to third-party hosts.</p>
<h2 data-u="mt6">Who else is involved</h2><ul><li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts the site and runs its server code. It processes each request (including your IP address, the page asked for and the time) and keeps operational logs. This Worker stores invocation logs with URL query strings redacted, and the rate limiter uses your IP address briefly to stop abuse.</li><li><strong>Yahoo Finance</strong> is the source of delayed quotes and price history. Our server fetches them; the stock symbol is sent to Yahoo, your browser is not.</li></ul>
<h2 data-u="mt6">Your choices</h2><p>To be removed from the email list, or to ask what is held about you, write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a> from the address concerned. Subscriptions stay in the list until removed. We accept deletion requests at this address. A fixed processing time and the host’s operational log retention period have not been published.</p>
<p class="src">21 November revision: clarified subscriber storage, delivery and browser export coverage. If this page and the site ever disagree, the site is wrong and we will fix it: tell us at the address above.</p></div></Base>
